Directory: FISSION
File:      actinides_inner_saddles_Bf1_WMM.readme (24 May 2026)
***************************************************************

                    ACTINIDES_INNER_SADDLES_BF1_WMM.DAT
First (inner) saddle-point properties and first (inner) fission barrier heights
               for 75 selected actinide isotopes with Z=89-98
        (Provided by P. Jachimowicz, M. Kowal, J. Skalski, 24 May 2026)
       *****************************************************************

Contents
--------
The file contains properties of the first (inner) saddle point and first (inner) fission barrier heights for 75 selected
actinide nuclei with Z=89-98. It provides masses, total energies, macroscopic and microscopic energy contributions, the corresponding
deformation parameters at the first (inner) saddle point, and the calculated first (inner) fission barrier heights. A search for saddle
points was performed using the “imaginary water flow” method in a five-dimensional deformation space including nonaxial shapes,
while reflection-asymmetric ones were found to have a negligible effect in this case. Further details of the model and computational
procedure can be found in Ref. [1].

Format
------
Each record of the file contains

     Z      : proton (charge) number
     N      : neutron number
     A      : mass number
     M      : saddle-point mass excess [MeV]
     Etot   : total saddle-point energy [MeV]
     Emac   : macroscopic saddle-point energy [MeV]
     Emic   : microscopic saddle-point energy [MeV]
     b2-b8  : deformation parameters at the first (inner) saddle point
     Bf1    : first (inner) static fission barrier height [MeV]

The corresponding Fortran format specification is (3i4,10f8.2).

References
----------
[1] P. Jachimowicz, M. Kowal, J. Skalski, At. Data Nucl. Data Tables 138, 101393 (2021).
